        "region": "chat-area",
        "callout": "Your Pivot Table crash course starts here"
      },
      "narration": "Alright, here's the scenario. You're early in your career, maybe still in school, and your boss just dropped a spreadsheet on you with ten thousand rows of data. Ten. Thousand. Rows. And they want a summary by end of day. You don't know formulas. You don't know VLOOKUP. You're about to spiral. Don't. By the end of this lesson, you'll know that a Pivot Table is created by selecting your data, clicking Insert, then Pivot Table, and dragging fields into Rows and Values. That's it. That's the whole trick. Let's go.",
