      "id": "e04",
      "time_offset_ms": 44866,
      "type": "show_message",
      "target": "chat_demo",
      "params": {
        "text": "I have a spreadsheet with 10,000 rows of coffee shop sales \u2014 columns for Date, Store, Product, and Amount. My boss wants total sales by store. I don't know any formulas. What do I do?",
        "region": "prompt-1"
      },
      "narration": null,
      "transition": "continuation",
      "clears": [],
      "phases": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e04_pause",
      "time_offset_ms": 45316,
      "type": "pause",
      "target": null,
      "params": {
        "duration": 0.5
      },
      "narration": null,
      "transition": "continuation",
      "clears": [],
      "phases": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e05",
      "time_offset_ms": 46166,
      "type": "show_response",
      "target": "chat_demo",
      "params": {
        "text": "Don't panic \u2014 you need a Pivot Table. Here's the good news: no formulas required.\n\n**Your data has 4 columns:**\n\u2022 Date\n\u2022 Store\n\u2022 Product\n\u2022 Amount\n\n**What a Pivot Table does:**\nIt takes thousands of rows and instantly groups and totals them for you. You just tell it WHAT to group by and WHAT to add up.\n\nYou won't type a single formula. You'll just drag and drop field names into boxes. Excel does all the math.",
        "region": "response-1"
      },
      "narration": null,
      "transition": "continuation",
      "clears": [],
      "phases": []
    },
    {
